From ca5ffbcac8450bf8f19afa60cb4c8008b3131cba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sarath Sadasivan Pillai <sarathsp06@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:25:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] The window opens before the overview page's slow section is
 built

Opening a review's window waited for its overview page, and the page ran
`graphify update` over the whole repository (a change review's blast
radius) or built the Tree-sitter index (a repository review) before it
was written: 34 of the 38 seconds a 3,600-file repository took to show
its window (the loading screen stays until onDidInitializeLayout
resolves).

The page is now written at once with what is cheap, says the repository
is being indexed or the code graph is being built, and the slow section
is built afterwards, one build per review at a time; the page is written
again when it is ready, and the document view reloads it (it already
watches the file). A failed build settles the section with its fallback
so the page stops saying it is being built. Opening the page again while
a build runs shows the section built before, or the note.

Unit tests for the page's wording while the section is being built.
